{"kind":"assert","text":"Cut-short exact-read review head 34042856b98ad5e7e6523d7fcc8574a8aec51c6a, tree ebfd77a2f323821906694f0f7222001b66c1ff8b. Main 08a16dc6 already contains the first-press and refresh landings. This head changes seven MCP source/test paths and the two new record paths. Frozen source ebc1e608e2e29432f2120cd4c63989d755d894d5, tree 365e708ae18cc8b5748eaa4ac6fc06a607909853, is directly above that main. Only this note and manifest differ afterward; all production, tests, configuration and Card inputs remain byte-identical under the documentation follow-up rule.\n\nThe session keeps truncated answers for display and file actions but only complete answers satisfy another exact-read press. The next ordinary press therefore makes a new bounded call without reopening the view. A new answer replaces the same identity/read key in the existing four-place list. Complete answers still replay without another credential or signature. Reading or refreshing the existing view does not silently retry. The original stop text, omitted-path words and commit labels remain. A truncated byte-limited read may reach the same limit again; the change offers another attempt, not promised completion.\n\nThe current reader stays enabled only while its displayed answer is truncated. A lone View diff now keeps that ordinary reader control on the partial page. A complete current reader keeps its prior disabled behavior. Opaque server-retained actions, active view, cut, busy and unresolved-original gates remain, as do the service authority, target, captured-view, signing, custody and credential checks. No producer limit or diff renderer changes.\n\nThe complete-held branch now checks the bounded projection result. If it cannot show the retained answer, it returns an error, no held:true claim, the same page and cut, and a receipt that says no new request was signed. It retains the answer for a later fitting projection and clears that specific refusal on successful replay. The existing new-answer refusal still says the credential is spent.\n\nThe whole 19-case session owner passes. Two new cases use scripted source/read ports at this retention boundary: a stopped interdiff then completion then no-call replay, and a complete held answer that stops fitting then recovers without another call. The real browser DOM, bridge, service, session and TEST scope signature/custody path run a scripted stopped Git answer followed by completion at 592 and 320 pixels. The first and next ordinary presses make exactly two read-token signatures; complete replay makes no third. Both screenshots show the original cutoff and omitted-path words and received visual inspection.\n\nThree controls distinguish by assertion. Reusing a truncated answer fails the next-call assertion; ignoring the fit result fails the error assertion; disabling the current truncated reader fails isEnabled before any click or timeout. Normal cases and every original deadline remain. The mutant browser stops at 592 pixels and leaves its later 320 case unreached; the normal driver passes both. Exact source/generated bytes restore. Local draft stages remain qualified, and the controls rerun the normal owner after all source changes.\n\nActual frozen full gate.exit is 0 and terminal source guards match clean ebc1e608. Every stage passes: Node 132, Counting 56, plain 3567 with one skip, Native 1029 with two skips. Counts come from terminal output, not optional progress. Exact-source Card workflow 41433119112 succeeds with generated-resource integrity and all three browser scripts. Raw whole Native and CI logs stay private with byte counts and hashes.\n\nManifest SHA256 e251530ed372bb15fe159676608abd5bf5feb0f012420323bd9a29c3b16afb8a verifies all 139 readonly files in six units and all thirteen output citations. The note is 11827 bytes; the manifest 26160 bytes. Final whitespace, commit, note and link checks all exit 0; all three local links resolve. Separate readonly final-review SHA256SUMS is 2d735ac0523d73e158bb603dbd33d1d63d86d4bc4a18ea616e2a7085c3ec0e2f. No deployment or Goose Desktop acceptance follows. Goose native control has recovered, but a custom extension registration awaits the user's action-time approval; that investigation stays under 1a44f042.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}